# Rust build artifacts
/target/

# disarm.h is generated reproducibly:
#   cargo test --features headers -- generate_headers
#
# It is COMMITTED, not ignored (#580). The header IS the C ABI contract, and a
# generated-and-discarded header cannot be diffed — the smoke test regenerates it and
# compiles against it in the same step, so a signature change plus a matching call-site
# change is self-consistent and passes. Committing the header makes every ABI change a
# visible diff a human has to approve, the same way src/metadata.rs and
# generated/parity.yaml are committed and drift-checked rather than regenerated blind.

# Compiled smoke-test binaries
*.o
